              "> **This skill covers the routing side of auth.** Route guards are UX and navigation control; the data/API boundary still belongs in the server function, server route, or API endpoint that reads or mutates private data. For the **server-side primitives** \u2014 session cookies (`HttpOnly`/`Secure`/`SameSite`), `useSession`-style helpers, OAuth `state` + PKCE, password-reset enumeration defense, CSRF, rate limiting \u2014 see [start-core/auth-server-primitives](../../../../start-client-core/skills/start-core/auth-server-primitives/SKILL.md).",
              ">"
            ]
          },
